#Adobe Acrobat DC
*.pdf

# PROPOSED CHANGE (not enacted — decide and edit by hand):
#   `*.pdf` above is repo-wide and silently swallows legitimate PDF deliverables
#   (design docs, manual renders, vendor datasheets). Nothing warns you; `git add`
#   just no-ops. Scope it to the directory that actually needed it, e.g.:
#       # /*.pdf                      # root-only Acrobat scratch
#       # docs/manual/_export/*.pdf   # generated manual renders
#   To find what the rule was hiding before you narrow it:
#       git ls-files -- '*.pdf'                   # already-tracked (unaffected by ignore)
#       git ls-files -o -i --exclude-standard -- '*.pdf'   # untracked+ignored, ALL depths
#   Use `ls-files -o -i`, NOT `git status --ignored --porcelain`: status defaults to
#   --ignored=traditional -unormal, which collapses a wholly-ignored directory to a
#   single `!! dir/` entry. PDFs under scratch/, docs/, node_modules/ or .worktrees/
#   would never be listed, so the enumeration under-reports and you would conclude
#   the broad rule hides nothing. (Verified: 1 of 3 ignored PDFs shown vs 3 of 3.)
#   Leaving the broad rule in place is a data-loss-by-omission risk, not just noise.

# CMO manual — rendered page images (large, regenerable via docs/manual/generate.py)
docs/manual/assets/images/

# PostScript / EPS exports (ImageMagick + Ghostscript intermediates; multi-MB,
# regenerable). Covers correctly-named future exports.
# Note 1: `*.ps` does NOT match `*.ps1` — tools/*.ps1 stay tracked.
# Note 2: the current 13.6 MB offender at repo root is named `re` (no extension),
#         so these patterns do NOT catch it. unity-housekeeping.sh quarantines it.
#         No extensionless root rule is added — too easy to hide real files.
*.ps
*.eps

# Mono runtime crash dumps (~10 MB each; written next to the working dir on
# Editor/player crashes. Regenerated on demand — never commit.)
# `mono_crash.*` already matches the 17 real offenders (mono_crash.mem.<pid>.blob).
# A bare `*.blob` is deliberately NOT added: it is redundant here and would
# silently mask any legitimately-tracked .blob asset added later — the same
# masking risk this file rejects for `*_snapshot.cs`, `*.patch` and extensionless
# root files.
mono_crash.*

# CMO DB crawler raw data
tools/cmano-db-crawler/_raw/

# Ephemeral nightly approve/import scratch (regenerable; may exceed GitHub 100MB limit)
scratch/

# Housekeeping quarantine — unity-housekeeping.sh moves ambiguous files here
# instead of deleting them. Contents are pending human review, never product.
# (Script lives at the repo root per UPGRADE-RUNBOOK.md; it self-locates with
# `git rev-parse --show-toplevel`, so it works from anywhere. CHANGESET.md says
# tools/ — reconcile the two before landing.)
_to_delete/

# NOTE: repo-root debug leftovers (panel_base_snapshot.cs, panel_head_snapshot.cs,
# pre_cesium_bridge.cs, panel_full_diff.patch) are deliberately NOT ignored.
# unity-housekeeping.sh quarantines them into _to_delete/, which clears git status
# without a rule. A `*_snapshot.cs` / `*.patch` ignore would mask the next
# accidental commit of a real source file, so no rule is added here.

