# PROPOSED CHANGE (not enacted — decide and edit by hand):
#   `.worktrees/` is declared three times (under "Superpowers parallel sprint
#   worktrees", "Unity Hub / smoke setup logs", and "Agent worktrees") plus a
#   separate `worktrees/`. Harmless to git, but it means three owners think they
#   own the rule and none of the comments is authoritative. Suggested collapse:
#   keep ONE block here —
#       # Git worktrees for parallel sprints (Superpowers + agent dispatch, local only)
#       .worktrees/
#       worktrees/
#   — and delete the copies at the two sections named above. Confirm `worktrees/`
#   is still in use (`ls -d worktrees .worktrees` on the host) before keeping it;
#   if it is dead, drop that line too rather than carrying both spellings.

